# InGame — environment configuration (SYS-03: env-only config, never hardcoded secrets).
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) for local dev. Real secrets live in the host secret store, never here.
#
# ── Key taxonomy (decision 0051/F04) — three buckets ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#  (1) SERVER-ONLY   — must NEVER reach the client bundle (DB creds, signing keys, SMTP, RC secret).
#  (2) INTENTIONAL-PUBLIC (EXPO_PUBLIC_*) — allow-listed by name in tools/security/bundle-grep.mjs;
#      these DO ship to every device by design (API base URL, Sentry DSN, RevenueCat PUBLIC key).
#  (3) Anything else matching a secret pattern in the built bundle FAILS the bundle-grep lint.
#  An EXPO_PUBLIC_*_SECRET / _KEY / _PASSWORD / _TOKEN name fails the lint (a mis-prefixed secret).

# ── (1) SERVER-ONLY ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Postgres connection string for the API. Local/staging/test DB names (or DISPOSABLE_DB=1) are the
# ONLY targets the destructive runners (migrate-down / reset / truncate) will touch (decision 0051/F03).
DATABASE_URL=postgres://ingame:ingame@localhost:5432/local_ingame

# Fail-closed sentinel for destructive DB operations (decision 0051/F03). Set to "1" ONLY on a
# disposable DB. Production creds structurally LACK this — the runner aborts without it.
DISPOSABLE_DB=1

# API server port.
PORT=4000

# Node environment.
NODE_ENV=development

# (M2) JWT signing secret, transactional-email transport key, RevenueCat SECRET key — server-only.
# JWT_SIGNING_SECRET=
# EMAIL_TRANSPORT_API_KEY=
# REVENUECAT_SECRET_KEY=

# ── (2) INTENTIONAL-PUBLIC (EXPO_PUBLIC_*) — allow-listed, ship to the client by design ───────────
# The API base URL the mobile client talks to.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4000/api
# (M2) Sentry DSN + RevenueCat PUBLIC SDK key are intentional-public; add them to the bundle-grep
# allow-list when wired:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_PUBLIC_KEY=
